-- The vocabulary every discovery name table starts with.
---
Spellings seeded into every discovery name table, in this exact order, so
their `NameId`s are pinned: index `i` of this list is the id of its spelling
in every table discovery builds.

This is a copy of the existing compiler's synthesized vocabulary
(`name_table_synthesized_spellings` in `compiler/stage_02_lex/name_table.brp`),
kept in the same order so the ids agree when the legacy adapter rebuilds that
compiler's frontend graph from these tables; the adapter asserts the two lists
are equal. It holds every keyword spelling, the names the parser and later
phases synthesize, the builtin callees subscript lowering names, the foreign
block argument names, and the first sixteen tuple field positions.
---
SEEDED_NAME_SPELLINGS: List[String] = [
	"",
	"func",
	"pure",
	"var",
	"union",
	"record",
	"void",
	"while",
	"for",
	"in",
